/**
 * What SB 634 did (inventory/review/sb634-consolidation-2026-10-04.md; Nathan, 4 October 2026: "Retire the Water Division
 * record, redirect it, and list it in the removed-records registry. Keep anything it held that the other records lack.
 * Then correct every place we said four bodies merged"; "All three get historical marks and all three sit under SCV Water as
 * predecessors").
 * The statute (Stats. 2017, ch. 833) reorganized two public bodies, the Castaic Lake Water Agency and the Newhall County Water
 * District, into the Santa Clarita Valley Water Agency, their successor. The Santa Clarita Water Division was the Castaic Lake
 * agency's retail division, with no separate existence; the Valencia Water Company was a private company whose stock the
 * agency had owned since December 2012, not a party to the reorganization, which the act directed the new agency to dissolve.
 *  1. Santa Clarita Water Division (#29567) retired: what it held goes into the Castaic Lake agency's text (the Bonelli
 *     companies, the 1999 purchase with its court date, the division); soft-deleted, redirected to the agency, registered.
 *  2. Valencia Water Company: its text rewritten from the statute and the court record; owned by the agency (parent), its
 *     assets passed to SCV Water on its dissolution (succeededBy), and it stays among SCV Water's predecessors as Nathan
 *     decided, its page saying it was not a party to the reorganization.
 *  3. Every "four bodies merged" corrected: SCV Water (#402), the consolidation event (#27712), the Newhall district (#27534),
 *     the Castaic Lake agency (#26563), Scott Wilk (#335, an unsourced import, the paragraph replaced and its unsourced claim of
 *     savings dropped). The footnotes quoting SCV Water's "merged three water agencies" give way to the statute.
 *  4. SCV Water: predecessors the Castaic Lake agency, the Newhall district and the Valencia company; its aliases cut to its
 *     own name.
 * Idempotent. Dry run by default. Set $APPLY = true to write.
 * Run: ddev craft exec "eval(file_get_contents('scripts/import/fix_sb634_two_bodies_2026_10_04.php'))"
 */
