$V_BODY = "The Valencia Water Company, incorporated on 7 April 1954, was the Newhall Land and Farming Company's private water company, regulated by the Public Utilities Commission, and one of the valley's retail water suppliers that bought their state water from the Castaic Lake Water Agency.[1] In December 2012 the agency bought all its stock from Newhall Land, by eminent domain on a settlement: its board resolved on 12 December, and the court entered judgment on 18 December. The company went on as a separate company owned by the agency. The Court of Appeal upheld the purchase in 2016, and the Newhall County Water District's suit over it was among the disputes the two public agencies settled by merging.[2][3]\n\nIt was not a party to the 2018 reorganization. Senate Bill 634 reorganized the Castaic Lake agency and the Newhall district into the Santa Clarita Valley Water Agency, which as the agency's successor became the company's owner, and directed the new agency to dissolve the company and take over its assets. The company's board approved a plan of dissolution on 28 December 2017, the new agency adopted it in January 2018, and the company's assets passed to SCV Water, which keeps a Valencia Water Division.[4][5][1]";
